WEBVTT

00:00:04.639 --> 00:00:10.939
<v Tomasz Nowak>Morning, everyone. Can you hear me? Right, Monday the 29th. Let's get through this before Teams decides otherwise.</v>

00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:19.670
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, got you. Traffic on the ring road was absolutely solid. I've spent longer looking at a bus than looking at production this morning.</v>

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.719
<v Jamie Brennan>Still less painful than the football last night.</v>

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:30.879
<v Callum Reid>Oh, don't start. Some of us were trying to forget that.</v>

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:37.469
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, football analysis closed. Anything already finished before we get into the live stuff?</v>

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:45.909
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, finished the repair on the IM3 last night. That's completed, not something carrying over into today.</v>

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.729
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good, that's off the live list then.</v>

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:55.469
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And I signed off the inspection on the WHB on Tuesday. That one's already done as well.</v>

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:06.420
<v Hannah Price>Just an observation from nights: noticed the Injection Moulding Line 1 was running a bit warm, but it settled down. Nothing new coming out of that.</v>

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:14.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Similar sort of thing, I heard a slight rattle from the GT2 bearing. Nothing to action yet, just saying what I heard.</v>

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:19.640
<v Tomasz Nowak>Okay, observations only. Neither of those is a fresh job from this meeting.</v>

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:30.040
<v Jamie Brennan>And I still can't get to the site water until production gives us a window. That's blocked, not something I can crack on with today.</v>

00:01:31.829 --> 00:01:34.629
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, there's no window agreed. That hasn't changed.</v>

00:01:36.819 --> 00:01:39.969
<v Tomasz Nowak>Understood. Leaving that blocked, no new commitment against it.</v>

00:01:41.359 --> 00:01:52.560
<v Tomasz Nowak>We need someone to do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve at half two. That's holding production up so it needs doing first. Anyone able to take it?</v>

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:59.420
<v Priya Raman>Um, I can't take that sign-off. Don't put it against me just because I've given the electrical update.</v>

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:06.239
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, understood. Nobody's taken it, then. It stays unowned; mentioning it isn't a sign-off.</v>

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:15.759
<v Sarah Okafor>And half two is still the required time, yeah. The production hold hasn't gone away just because we haven't got a name.</v>

00:02:16.889 --> 00:02:25.639
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah so, I'll schedule downtime for the 11kV board with production after lunch. Not an emergency but don't let it slip—that's how I'm treating it.</v>

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:31.990
<v Sarah Okafor>You're doing the scheduling after lunch, not saying the board's coming off after lunch?</v>

00:02:34.449 --> 00:02:40.050
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Exactly. I'll agree the downtime with production after lunch. I'm not announcing an outage time here.</v>

00:02:41.039 --> 00:02:43.840
<v Tomasz Nowak>Cheers, Olu. Scheduling with production is yours, then.</v>

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:53.000
<v Tomasz Nowak>For me, I'll go to Harbour Road Warehouse to pick up the replacement parts for the line 3 chiller on the 3rd.</v>

00:02:54.569 --> 00:02:57.370
<v Jamie Brennan>On the 3rd, right? Not a collection today?</v>

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:08.310
<v Tomasz Nowak>On the 3rd, yes. That one's safety critical, straight away—it's not a routine pickup to leave sitting about. The collection date is still the 3rd.</v>

00:03:10.069 --> 00:03:14.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Got it, Tomasz. Safety-critical collection, on the 3rd. Those two bits are clear.</v>

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:19.580
<v Callum Reid>I'll run the monthly fire alarm test after lunch.</v>

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:25.460
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, talking over you—monthly test, not the separate panel function test?</v>

00:03:26.819 --> 00:03:31.020
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, just the monthly fire alarm test. I'll do that after lunch.</v>

00:03:32.349 --> 00:03:34.099
<v Tomasz Nowak>Thanks, Callum. Separate entries, definitely.</v>

00:03:35.189 --> 00:03:41.490
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sarah, can you run a function test on the fire alarm panel next week? That's the other one.</v>

00:03:43.379 --> 00:03:47.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, I'll run the function test on the fire alarm panel next week.</v>

00:03:49.689 --> 00:03:55.990
<v Priya Raman>Good. I only asked because those two descriptions keep sounding like the same thing when the audio drops.</v>

00:03:56.759 --> 00:04:02.710
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, fair question. Monthly test after lunch; panel function test next week. Not doubling up the owners.</v>

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:08.800
<v Hannah Price>I'll check the guarding on the Injection Moulding Line 2 today at 2pm. It's urgent.</v>

00:04:11.099 --> 00:04:16.000
<v Callum Reid>Two o'clock, did you say? You went a bit robotic at the end there.</v>

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:23.550
<v Hannah Price>Today at 2pm, yeah. I'll take the guarding check, and it's urgent, not a routine look whenever.</v>

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:26.089
<v Tomasz Nowak>Got you, Hannah. That's clearly yours.</v>

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:34.879
<v Tomasz Nowak>The other gap is we need someone to swap the filter on the compressor one by end of day. Anyone taking that?</v>

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:41.620
<v Jamie Brennan>Not me. Just to be clear, being on the stores call isn't me volunteering to fit it.</v>

00:04:43.519 --> 00:04:45.620
<v Priya Raman>I can't take that one either.</v>

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:52.600
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right. Nobody on the filter swap, then. Still needed by end of day, still unallocated.</v>

00:04:54.959 --> 00:05:00.209
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, don't hide that with a vague 'maintenance' against it. We haven't agreed an owner.</v>

00:05:02.439 --> 00:05:07.339
<v Tomasz Nowak>Jamie, can you send the shift handover report round, whenever you get a chance?</v>

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:13.560
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll send the shift handover report round. Whenever I get a chance, understood.</v>

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:19.769
<v Hannah Price>That's just circulating the report, isn't it? Not another report we're all suddenly writing?</v>

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:25.250
<v Tomasz Nowak>Just sending it round. No extra bit of work for everyone tucked in there.</v>

00:05:25.959 --> 00:05:31.910
<v Jamie Brennan>Lovely. Yes, I'll take sending it. Nice to have one that doesn't involve chasing a delivery wagon.</v>

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:40.490
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sarah, can you grease and check the bearings on the booster pump? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:48.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, I'll grease and check the bearings on the booster pump. Not an emergency, but I won't let it slip.</v>

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.939
<v Olumide Adeyemi>That's separate from the rattle you mentioned earlier, yeah?</v>

00:05:55.790 --> 00:06:02.790
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, different thing. The GT2 bearing rattle is observation only, nothing to action yet. I'm accepting the booster pump job.</v>

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:15.100
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, urgent bits haven't changed: Boiler Safety Relief Valve sign-off at half two, holding production up, needs doing first, but no owner. Guarding check today at 2pm is urgent and has an owner.</v>

00:06:16.009 --> 00:06:21.259
<v Hannah Price>Yes, I've got the Injection Moulding Line 2 guarding check. No ambiguity on that one.</v>

00:06:22.639 --> 00:06:27.540
<v Tomasz Nowak>And Olu, the 11kV board scheduling after lunch—not an emergency, but not to drift.</v>

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:31.149
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, mine. I'll schedule it with production after lunch.</v>

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:41.949
<v Jamie Brennan>Just so the water doesn't get swept into that conversation, the site water is still blocked by the production window. No change from me.</v>

00:06:42.889 --> 00:06:46.040
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, agreed. We're not treating that as released work.</v>

00:06:48.439 --> 00:06:56.490
<v Priya Raman>And the IM3 repair is finished. I know we've gone round a few things twice, but that one really is off the list.</v>

00:06:58.129 --> 00:07:07.930
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep. Longer-dated ones: Sarah has the fire alarm panel function test next week, and I've got Harbour Road Warehouse for the line 3 chiller parts on the 3rd.</v>

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:14.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct, next week for my panel function test. Separate from Callum's monthly test after lunch.</v>

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:27.529
<v Tomasz Nowak>And we're ending with two explicit gaps: nobody for the Boiler Safety Relief Valve sign-off at half two, nobody for the compressor one filter swap by end of day. Neither is magically covered.</v>

00:07:28.079 --> 00:07:31.579
<v Jamie Brennan>Right. More honest than the commentary on that match, anyway.</v>

00:07:32.089 --> 00:07:37.339
<v Tomasz Nowak>You nearly made it to the end without mentioning it again. Cheers, everyone, that's us.</v>
